Pete Bevan: "Right, thanks Sian. Let's start with the two entries. I'll read the account out loud and we'll tick each line off against the bank statement so we both see the same thing. If the $165 and the $387 are duplicates, we need to know before Monday, because that rent is the one thing we can't be short on. Go on, read me the first line."
Sian Bevan: "Right, let's go through it line by line. I'm reading the household account now — the balance shown is $1,309.50. The first line is the $165 rent to Dunmore Lettings, and then there's the $387 entry. Let me check these against the statement before we tick anything off."
Pete Bevan: "Right, good. Before you read the lines out, here's what I want us to do. Read me the $165 entry and the $387 entry exactly as they appear, with dates and references, and I'll check each against the bank statement on my end. If the rent has gone out twice, we need to know which one actually cleared. And Sian, don't tick anything off yet. Just read the two lines to me."

